# Canonical Branch and Deployment

- Use `main` for development, integration, pushes, and production deployments in both repositories.
- Do not create or switch to another branch unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Fetch all refs before completion and merge every relevant task branch that is ahead of `main`.
- Treat `master` only as a legacy fast-forward mirror; never develop on it or deploy from it.
- Never force-push canonical or mirror refs.
- Deploy only exact commits that passed the applicable backend, unit, and browser workflow gates.
- Verify the exact live revision and OIDC/authenticated browser smoke after deployment.
